      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While 30% headcount reduction sounds appealing for the bottom line, rushing expensive infrastructure deployments before confirming the technology's long-term ROI often leads to hidden maintenance costs and operational bottlenecks. Investing in human training rather than immediate replacement usually preserves institutional knowledge and keeps the company agile if the technology shifts, which often results in higher sustainable profits over the long term than a one-time payroll cut. The board will likely appreciate a conservative, data-driven strategy that balances immediate efficiency with risk mitigation rather than relying on a guaranteed mathematical model that often ignores real-world complexity.",
